      "output": "**Static review: I only read the two reports and the specs. Nothing was run here.**\n\n**After the second pass: not actually run.** Both reports end with \"Fixes: in progress\", so there is no result for the page after pass 2's fixes. The latest measured state is pass 2's first check of the page pass 1 delivered: **49/61 passed**, 0 page errors, blank check not measured (screenshot timed out), self-test 15,769 ms.\n\n**Still failing:** T15 dressing, T16 castle, T23 input, T28 anim, T32 combat, T33 combat, T35 fighter, T37 player, T39 player, T42 ai, T53 audio, T57 hud.\n\n**Planted failures:** 21/23 caught on the first check, then 25/26. P05 (render, fog) was missed on the first check and caught on the next. **P03 (anim, uniform rate) is still not caught**, though T29, the test meant to catch it, is not listed as failing. That conflict is unresolved.\n\n**What the fixes changed:** neither report says what code changed. From the results alone:\n- **Pass 1:** these went from failing to passing: T7, T8, T9 (render), T14 (dressing), T25, T27 (camera), T34 (fighter), T49–T51 (fx, now registered), T54 (audio), and T61, which has no owner because the spec lists only 60 tests. The 3 init errors (`insertBefore`, two `null.add`) are gone. Self-test time went from 4.4 s to 15.8 s.\n- **Pass 2:** no effect reported (not actually run).\n\n**Counts that don't match the spec:** 61 tests against 60 in B7; 23, then 26 plants against 16 in B8.\n\n**Spec parts no test covers:**\n- weather re-roll, storm, the full day cycle\n- most combos and arts; ripostes, backstabs, burning, knockdown\n- jump and mantle\n- arbalist and crawler behaviour; boss move effects\n- touch, gamepad flicks, pointer-lock fallback\n- pause, inventory, equipment, settings, credits; map relief\n- frame budget, adaptive pixel ratio, LOD streaming, boot and asset-settle times\n- play time\n\n**Assets:** the reports say nothing about assets. The spec (B9) says real GLBs are absent in the sandbox and stand-ins run the tests. T4–T6 (asset tests) are not listed as failing, which suggests the stand-in path passed, but this isn't shown directly. Whether stand-in measurements match real clips is unknown, because T28 (animation measurement) fails. Real models in the live preview: not actually run.\n",
